    "$comment": "SMOODEV-2619 — cross-language parity corpus for the audit hash chain. This file is the SINGLE committed source of truth that BOTH the TS serializer (packages/audit/src/hash-chain.ts) and the Rust serializer (rust/audit-worker/src/canonical.rs) assert against. Each fixture's `event` is the pre-hash event object (the AuditEvent minus `hashCurrent`, with `hashPrevious` set or omitted) that is fed to computeEventHash / compute_event_hash. `expectedCanonical` is the byte-exact canonical JSON both must produce; `expectedHash` is the SHA-256 hex of those bytes. If TS and Rust ever disagree here the hash chain is broken across stores — do NOT 'fix' a divergence by editing hashes; investigate the serializer. Expected values are generated by the real TS serializer (see the ADR-089 groundwork PR); regenerate only when the fixture EVENTS intentionally change.",
